1
00:00:06,680 --> 00:00:08,277
You monsters!

2
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,240
Don't turn your backs on me!

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,830
Find it!

4
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,640
I'll favor this one!

5
00:00:15,940 --> 00:00:17,520
Hamon Baby Launcher!

6
00:00:36,440 --> 00:00:37,380
Thank you.

7
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:06,200
Thank you.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:32,637
I'll be in love with the enemy.

9
00:01:32,720 --> 00:01:36,077
I'll be in love with the lack of hope.

10
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:41,060
I'll be in love with you.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,830
Could this be...

12
00:02:00,913 --> 00:02:02,720
is this what I think? Nice work!

13
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:06,157
Caesar may be a narcissist,
but his Hamon skills are solid.

14
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:10,700
These bubbles may look harmless,
but prepare for a bombardment!

15
00:02:20,200 --> 00:02:21,030
He...

16
00:02:21,113 --> 00:02:21,943
he popped them all.

17
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:23,747
How on earth did he do that?

18
00:02:23,960 --> 00:02:25,136
That's not his hair.

19
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:27,897
Those are wires attached to
his head he's manipulating.

20
00:02:27,980 --> 00:02:31,340
He pumped my bubbles with
the wind that they created.

21
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:35,660
But then that means they were
designed to be anti-Harmon weapons.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,537
Somehow they're already familiar
with the principles of Harmon.

23
00:02:39,620 --> 00:02:44,100
They must have faced Harmon at
some point over 2,000 years ago.

24
00:02:46,140 --> 00:02:47,220
What is that?

25
00:02:47,480 --> 00:02:49,833
What's happening to the air around them?

26
00:02:50,140 --> 00:02:52,520
Caesar, look out! Get down!

27
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:55,520
What the...

28
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:58,440
Cover your eyes!

29
00:02:58,640 --> 00:02:59,817
That wasn't just wind,

30
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:03,547
it was the aftermath of a powerful
vortex that's still active!

31
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,330
Caesar!

32
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,640
These humans know Hamon.

33
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:14,317
I thought we destroyed all the members of
the Hamon tribe two thousand years ago.

34
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:18,224
And yet, here they are, ready to
welcome us at our own awakening.

35
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:22,290
Damn!

36
00:03:22,373 --> 00:03:24,860
You killed him!

37
00:03:25,320 --> 00:03:26,700
You killed my friend!

38
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:29,900
Do you think losing him high will stop me?

39
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,110
Stop!

40
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,297
Why are you laughing?

41
00:03:36,380 --> 00:03:37,321
What's so funny?

42
00:03:38,540 --> 00:03:41,658
You all have memorized your
Hamon handbook very well.

43
00:03:41,960 --> 00:03:43,900
You always say the same thing.

44
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:46,497
It was that way when we crossed
from the western continent.

45
00:03:46,580 --> 00:03:48,520
And it is that way now still.

46
00:03:48,960 --> 00:03:52,640
Do you think losing an arm or
an eye or a leg will stop me?

47
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:54,777
How dare you take my friend's life?

48
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:56,757
Don't you know how much I loved him?

49
00:03:56,840 --> 00:04:00,560
That's why we laugh,
human. You! You bastards!

50
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,070
Ignore him.

51
00:04:02,153 --> 00:04:04,159
We're on a quest to find the stone.

52
00:04:04,560 --> 00:04:05,390
What?

53
00:04:05,473 --> 00:04:06,303
Where are you going?

54
00:04:06,386 --> 00:04:07,560
Face me, cowards!

55
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:13,998
You're most vulnerable in
your throat and your lungs.

56
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:18,057
We know that if you can't breathe,
then your hormone is rendered useless.

57
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:21,420
But because I cannot resist
a worthy opponent, hear me.

58
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:24,737
I shall spare you because I long for the

59
00:04:24,820 --> 00:04:27,879
opportunity to meet you
again when you are stronger.

60
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:31,400
The next time we meet, I
want to admire your strength.

61
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:36,900
I want you to become worthy of my time so
that I might destroy you with great honor.

62
00:04:44,840 --> 00:04:47,487
It appears that he was
the only Hormone user.

63
00:04:48,460 --> 00:04:49,401
Hmm, let's move.

64
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,277
Sorry, I just can't seem
to shake this cough.

65
00:04:58,360 --> 00:05:00,797
Maybe it's the Hormone
training that's making me ill.

66
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:01,939
What do you think?

67
00:05:04,460 --> 00:05:06,740
Hmm, he only sliced your eyelid.

68
00:05:06,940 --> 00:05:09,234
The actual eyeball itself is just fine.

69
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,337
Perhaps you should sit this one out.

70
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:14,477
I think we've all seen enough of
the Bubble Launcher for one day.

71
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:17,237
Watch and learn as I take
care of this one myself!

72
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:18,150
JoJo!

73
00:05:18,233 --> 00:05:19,488
Just calm down, Speedwagon.

74
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:21,560
This guy is asking for it.

75
00:05:21,780 --> 00:05:24,777
It's time for me to show off the brand
new technique I've been working on.

76
00:05:24,860 --> 00:05:25,690
What?

77
00:05:25,773 --> 00:05:27,758
Please allow me to introduce myself.

78
00:05:28,080 --> 00:05:29,720
My name is Joseph Joestar,

79
00:05:30,040 --> 00:05:33,864
and these are the hands known for
defeating your mate-son Viento.

80
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:43,020
I call this move my hum-on-clacker volley.

81
00:05:43,220 --> 00:05:47,691
I start off by filling these little
clacker balls here with a bit of Hamon.

82
00:05:55,080 --> 00:05:56,080
Oh, no!

83
00:05:56,780 --> 00:05:58,957
JoJo, what the hell do
you think you're doing?

84
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,569
This is no time for games.

85
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:01,717
What are you doing?

86
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:05,271
Are you trying to disrespect
my friend by playing the fool?

87
00:06:05,380 --> 00:06:06,500
Not intentionally.

88
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:08,360
I'm trying to be serious.

89
00:06:08,820 --> 00:06:11,960
Caesar, I am truly sorry
for the loss of your friend.

90
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:14,709
I understand both your
pain and your anger.

91
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:15,930
Additionally,

92
00:06:16,013 --> 00:06:17,637
these guys may be the biggest group of

93
00:06:17,720 --> 00:06:20,620
egotistical jackasses
I've ever seen in my life.

94
00:06:20,780 --> 00:06:22,697
I may not be a master of this yet,

95
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:26,662
but I'll still knock you into next
Tuesday with my clacker volley!

96
00:06:29,900 --> 00:06:33,665
I hate to admit it, but I know
that my Heaven is relatively weak.

97
00:06:33,780 --> 00:06:37,197
I'm pretty sure I can make up for what
I'm lacking with these steel clackers

98
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:40,777
if I can just break open your scheme
even a little and fill you with Heaven.

99
00:06:40,860 --> 00:06:43,257
That should even up my
handicap, don't you think?

100
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:44,869
I can tell you're nervous.

101
00:06:45,520 --> 00:06:46,400
Take that!

102
00:06:55,360 --> 00:06:56,700
Well, that was fun.

103
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:57,998
Let us keep moving.

104
00:06:58,520 --> 00:07:01,877
Apparently, the human race has
regressed rather than evolved.

105
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,372
Quite an understatement.

106
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:08,041
Amusing, though.

107
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:11,200
Jojo, what are you doing?

108
00:07:11,420 --> 00:07:14,077
Your child's little games are
going to get us all killed.

109
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:17,866
He's playing coy, but this may
actually be the best JoJo's got.

110
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:21,037
He'd be fine if he was facing
some common street punk,

111
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:23,097
but I don't think he realizes that these

112
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:25,557
opponents are on a
completely different level.

113
00:07:25,640 --> 00:07:28,280
It would be comical if
it weren't so tragic.

114
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:31,757
Why isn't anyone taking my
little metal balls seriously?

115
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:32,960
That's far enough.

116
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:35,533
Don't make me clack you into the ground.

117
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:36,810
Stop.

118
00:07:36,893 --> 00:07:39,177
Don't you feel that human
lives are short enough?

119
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:41,037
There's no need to sprint to your death.

120
00:07:41,120 --> 00:07:41,950
Silence!

121
00:07:42,033 --> 00:07:45,657
If you've ever had spaghetti on nero
de sepia, you know it looks bad,

122
00:07:45,740 --> 00:07:46,858
but it's delicious.

123
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:50,235
You should taste my clacker
volley before you judge it.

124
00:07:54,900 --> 00:07:57,180
The clackers, they vanished!

125
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:03,740
I've been training on my
harmon all the live long day.

126
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:05,780
He's insane!

127
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:10,880
Well, look at Ma, no hands.

128
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,473
Where are the clackers?

129
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,920
A true magician.

130
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:18,220
Never reveals his secrets! Ain't this!

131
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:27,280
How can anything move like that?

132
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:29,017
I can't believe what I'm seeing.

133
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:30,747
He's faster than San Viento.

134
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:34,527
I don't think those idiotic
clackers did so much as graze him.

135
00:08:35,240 --> 00:08:39,280
I admire your weapon, your courage,
and your creativity, human.

136
00:08:40,640 --> 00:08:43,557
I'm actually enjoying
your company you deserve

137
00:08:43,640 --> 00:08:47,617
time one minute but only one that is how

138
00:08:47,700 --> 00:08:49,937
much Time I will allow
you to fight the mighty

139
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:56,237
Wamuu I shall use your

140
00:08:56,320 --> 00:08:57,997
wound as a timer your

141
00:08:58,080 --> 00:09:00,337
wrist will work well
as a timekeeping device

142
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:02,737
and you will lose
consciousness due to a loss

143
00:09:02,820 --> 00:09:06,737
of blood in exactly one
minute show me what you

144
00:09:06,820 --> 00:09:10,817
can do human oh this is
what I often told the

145
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:13,657
members of the Hamon
tribe your life is now

146
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:17,357
my hourglass measured
in blood Wamuu we'll be

147
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:20,817
waiting outside now boy
go ahead and retrieve

148
00:09:20,900 --> 00:09:24,457
your weapon quickly What
I'm sorry I'm growing

149
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:27,197
deaf in this ear it
almost sounded like you

150
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:29,877
said go ahead and
retrieve your weapon which

151
00:09:29,960 --> 00:09:32,397
would be ridiculous I
mean why would you to

152
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:35,304
retrieve something that
comes right back to you.

153
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:47,997
Looks like my clack of
boomerang worked pretty well.

154
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:51,433
I shouldn't even need the full
minute to destroy you now.

155
00:09:51,980 --> 00:09:53,897
That's for killing Caesar's friend.

156
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:56,037
That's for not taking me seriously.

157
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:59,473
And that's because I'm sick
of looking at your ugly face.

158
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:00,937
Do what you must.

159
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:02,500
I deserve as much.

160
00:10:02,740 --> 00:10:07,317
No opponent has ever struck my face, and
this is the price for my carelessness.

161
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:11,988
I shall take this beating in order to
properly honor you before I destroy you.

162
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:24,166
You say that no one has ever hit
you in that ugly mug of yours?

163
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:25,860
What an honor!

164
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:31,537
You didn't even stop to blink when you
killed Caesar's friend, Mark, did you?

165
00:10:31,620 --> 00:10:32,450
You monster!

166
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,520
Do you not value life at all?

167
00:10:35,100 --> 00:10:36,400
Jojo, watch yourself!

168
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:37,817
His arm isn't broken!

169
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:39,606
He's getting ready to use it!

170
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:46,750
Whoa!

171
00:10:46,833 --> 00:10:48,717
I have a feeling this isn't good for me.

172
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:51,040
A charming observation, human.

173
00:10:51,460 --> 00:10:53,677
I'm now scarred due to my carelessness.

174
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:58,642
It was my duty to allow you to pummel me
as punishment for my own lack of judgment.

175
00:10:59,020 --> 00:11:00,800
That has now ended, however.

176
00:11:01,160 --> 00:11:03,572
Jojo, finish him now while you still can!

177
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:07,960
My ultimate technique,
the Divine Sandstorm!

178
00:11:08,540 --> 00:11:10,357
I don't like the sound of that!

179
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:13,087
He starts by spinning
his left arm clockwise,

180
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,652
and then his right arm counter-clockwise.

181
00:11:16,040 --> 00:11:18,537
Jojo is unprepared to
counter a technique like

182
00:11:18,620 --> 00:11:21,561
this as Wamo's fists seem
to grow before his eyes.

183
00:11:24,560 --> 00:11:29,320
The air between Whamu's arms transforms
into a powerful vortex of destruction.

184
00:11:29,760 --> 00:11:33,231
This vacuum creates a highly
pressurized, deadly maelstrom.

185
00:11:35,720 --> 00:11:38,117
Great, if he can tear
through marble pillars,

186
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:41,597
I don't see myself having much of a
chance against a windstorm like this.

187
00:11:41,680 --> 00:11:44,739
I don't think I've ever
seen anything this powerful!

188
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:50,510
Jojo!

189
00:11:57,540 --> 00:12:00,020
I call that Divine Sandstorm.

190
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:02,360
No! Jojo!

191
00:12:02,820 --> 00:12:04,055
Don't be a damn fool!

192
00:12:04,240 --> 00:12:05,420
Run, Speedwagon.

193
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,457
Get out of here before it's too late.

194
00:12:07,540 --> 00:12:09,540
I'll try and distract him somehow.

195
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:11,768
Curse this blood in my eye.

196
00:12:11,920 --> 00:12:12,897
Threw off my aim.

197
00:12:12,980 --> 00:12:17,098
But it proved enough when you made
the choice to hide behind a pillar.

198
00:12:17,860 --> 00:12:18,690
Hmm.

199
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:20,460
You died quickly.

200
00:12:21,420 --> 00:12:24,949
Normally, I would ignore human
onlookers such as yourselves.

201
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,230
However,

202
00:12:26,320 --> 00:12:31,144
you witnessed my shame, so unfortunately
I must take the time to destroy you both.

203
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:33,320
You may pray now if you wish.

204
00:12:36,360 --> 00:12:37,190
Huh?

205
00:12:41,880 --> 00:12:43,700
Hmm, must be the light.

206
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:50,020
What does he think he's doing?

207
00:12:50,460 --> 00:12:52,100
I don't believe it.

208
00:12:52,260 --> 00:12:54,084
He's actually trying to escape!

209
00:12:57,900 --> 00:12:59,180
Huh? Hmm...

210
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:03,780
That coward has no shame
playing dead like that.

211
00:13:03,980 --> 00:13:07,320
I understand leaving me,
but what about Speedwagon?

212
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,100
I knew he was spineless!

213
00:13:09,640 --> 00:13:12,800
This guy is the most
powerful foe I've ever faced.

214
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:14,884
My breathing is out of control.

215
00:13:14,980 --> 00:13:16,720
I can't control my Hamon.

216
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:19,511
I don't really have any other option left.

217
00:13:19,860 --> 00:13:22,640
Luckily, my specialty is running away.

218
00:13:23,920 --> 00:13:26,200
Behold, our now broken hero.

219
00:13:26,840 --> 00:13:28,460
Jojo, forced to play dead,

220
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:33,447
crawling for his life, and now leaving
Speedwagon behind to face certain death.

221
00:13:33,780 --> 00:13:38,540
Even with all of this, Jojo remains
dedicated, a hero worthy of this tale.

222
00:13:38,900 --> 00:13:40,200
How is that, you ask?

223
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:46,220
Nice try there, human.

224
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:48,820
You coward.

225
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:52,829
No true warrior would ever feign
death just to save himself.

226
00:13:56,960 --> 00:14:01,195
That may be true, though my intention
was not to escape but to distract.

227
00:14:01,460 --> 00:14:04,917
Truth be told, I was just trying
to get you onto this minecart.

228
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,480
You are clever indeed.

229
00:14:06,900 --> 00:14:10,777
So you were only playing the part of the
coward to lure me away from your friends,

230
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:11,690
is that right?

231
00:14:11,773 --> 00:14:13,157
I'm surprised you fell for it.

232
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,237
That trick is probably older than you.

233
00:14:15,320 --> 00:14:17,200
Get out now, speed wagon. Run!

234
00:14:17,640 --> 00:14:18,470
Caesar, go!

235
00:14:18,553 --> 00:14:19,892
What are you guys doing?

236
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,740
Jojo, that bastard.

237
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,240
What a noble move.

238
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:28,317
Now that I've painted
myself into a corner here,

239
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:31,117
I need to come up with a
second part to my plan,

240
00:14:31,200 --> 00:14:32,480
which would be...

241
00:14:35,900 --> 00:14:37,400
The unflappable hero.

242
00:14:37,680 --> 00:14:40,697
He calmly searches for options,
not knowing what to do next,

243
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,580
but his will remains unbroken.

244
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:44,290
Jojo! No!

245
00:14:45,680 --> 00:14:46,920
Damn you, Jojo!

246
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,480
He's in far worse shape than I am!

247
00:14:50,760 --> 00:14:53,466
I should have been the
one to lure Wamuu away.

248
00:14:53,660 --> 00:14:57,484
I see now that Jojo only acts
foolishly to confound his opponent.

249
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:01,033
He must actually have a good
plan to beat those monsters.

250
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:12,337
Although you are quite confident for
someone who is knocking on death's door?

251
00:15:12,420 --> 00:15:15,067
I must tell you that
your plan is a poor one.

252
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:17,657
You're quite tough, I'll give you that.

253
00:15:17,740 --> 00:15:19,799
Soft-headed, but tough nonetheless.

254
00:15:20,420 --> 00:15:24,337
Tell me, how do you remain unyielding
in the moments before your death?

255
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:28,457
Is it because you have bricks for brains,
or do you still have another trick for me?

256
00:15:28,540 --> 00:15:32,200
Do you really want to know?
Actually, no. Let me guess.

257
00:15:32,480 --> 00:15:34,337
Because you're so obviously clever,

258
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:36,537
I'll give you the benefit of
the doubt that you wouldn't be

259
00:15:36,620 --> 00:15:39,997
stupid enough to be holding a
stick of dynamite behind your back.

260
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:41,197
Damn, he's on to me!

261
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:44,597
And I know you wouldn't insult my
intelligence by thinking you could

262
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:47,677
quickly throw the brake and send
the minecart flying off the tracks.

263
00:15:47,760 --> 00:15:48,720
Maybe like this!

264
00:15:52,740 --> 00:15:54,300
Damn, he got me there too!

265
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:01,860
The time on your hourglass
wrist is just about up.

266
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:06,100
There is absolutely no chance that
you will survive this any longer.

267
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:09,140
I found your tricks to be very quaint.

268
00:16:10,880 --> 00:16:15,200
Before you die, tell me, why do I
still not see defeat in your eyes?

269
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:19,597
I'll tell you if you want, but you're
going to have to say please first.

270
00:16:19,680 --> 00:16:20,510
More games!

271
00:16:20,593 --> 00:16:21,897
You've tested me long enough.

272
00:16:21,980 --> 00:16:23,860
Prepare to die! Such a shame,

273
00:16:24,020 --> 00:16:28,549
because a month from now I can guarantee
that I would be able to destroy you.

274
00:16:30,520 --> 00:16:31,400
What was that?

275
00:16:31,580 --> 00:16:35,057
With just one more month of
training, I would annihilate you.

276
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:39,057
I was the first person to hit as
well as the first to scar your face.

277
00:16:39,140 --> 00:16:43,316
When I put my mind to something, I
can accomplish pretty much anything.

278
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:48,581
Oh, well, I guess none of
that really matters now.

279
00:16:48,820 --> 00:16:51,220
So, can we just get this over with?

280
00:16:51,580 --> 00:16:55,874
It will be an honor to be killed by
a warrior like you, blah, blah, blah.

281
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:58,191
What do you mean by this?

282
00:16:58,440 --> 00:17:00,969
Oh, I'm sick and tired
of all this talking.

283
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:03,437
Just hurry up and make it painless, Wamu.

284
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,517
Explain yourself.

285
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:06,365
What are you trying to get at?

286
00:17:14,340 --> 00:17:16,740
I don't know how, but he's still alive.

287
00:17:17,340 --> 00:17:20,634
Is it true that you Pillar
Men often live for millennia?

288
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:22,977
That's a long time to be
walking around with the

289
00:17:23,060 --> 00:17:26,236
shame of having your face
rearranged by a lowly human.

290
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:29,857
It seems to me that the only way
you could regain your honor would be

291
00:17:29,940 --> 00:17:33,777
by defeating me in a fight after
I've undergone proper Hamon training.

292
00:17:33,860 --> 00:17:37,340
I do not have to defeat you
in order to maintain my honor.

293
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,440
His entire body is shaking with rage.

294
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:44,137
I have a chance if I can make him
think his integrity is at stake.

295
00:17:44,220 --> 00:17:48,857
He gave himself away as the proud warrior
type the moment he called me a coward.

296
00:17:48,940 --> 00:17:50,587
Pride is his Achilles' heel.

297
00:17:50,880 --> 00:17:53,717
I don't know if you noticed,
but I'm still new at this.

298
00:17:53,800 --> 00:17:55,997
However, if I trained with
my harmon for a month,

299
00:17:56,080 --> 00:17:59,517
I know I could give you the fair
fight a warrior like you deserves.

300
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:03,117
The first person who ever hit you
in the face gave you a nasty scar.

301
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:07,024
It would be a shame if you killed
that person before he's worthy.

302
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:10,477
But if you feel the need to kill me before

303
00:18:10,560 --> 00:18:12,657
I have a chance to battle you as an equal,

304
00:18:12,740 --> 00:18:15,387
then go ahead and do
whatever you need to do.

305
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,760
You bastard!

306
00:18:19,980 --> 00:18:20,810
Mama.

307
00:18:20,893 --> 00:18:21,723
Master ACDC.

308
00:18:21,806 --> 00:18:23,557
You gave this human one minute.

309
00:18:23,640 --> 00:18:26,464
Why must you insist on
letting him toy with you?

310
00:18:26,820 --> 00:18:27,900
Just go away.

311
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:29,080
I almost had him.

312
00:18:40,220 --> 00:18:44,691
Master ACDC, I have grown fond of this
particular member of the Hamon tribe.

313
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,360
I got him!

314
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:50,957
Jojo, you will be happy to know that I
have decided to accept your proposition.

315
00:18:51,040 --> 00:18:54,397
If you swear that you will train your
hardest to fulfill your potential,

316
00:18:54,480 --> 00:18:57,257
then I will give you
exactly one month to do so.

317
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:59,357
So you're not going to kill me now?

318
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:00,270
That's right.

319
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:03,180
But we're going to fight again. We are.

320
00:19:03,540 --> 00:19:05,217
Are you sure you want to do this?

321
00:19:05,300 --> 00:19:07,257
I'll give you a chance to take it back.

322
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,620
Yes, I can't believe it's working.

323
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:15,100
However, I will need assurances that you
will not try to run away again, of course.

324
00:19:16,040 --> 00:19:17,020
Nice, Wamu.

325
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:19,477
I was wondering when you
would finally propose.

326
00:19:19,560 --> 00:19:21,860
Say hello to the wedding ring of death.

327
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,336
Guess where it goes.

328
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,180
A hint not on your finger.

329
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,880
What are you doing with that?

330
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:33,380
This ring will start
to dissolve in 33 days.

331
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:38,805
It's impossible to remove, and once
dissolved, it will release a virulent poison.

332
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:43,336
Any attempt to remove or damage it
will also release the lethal poison.

333
00:19:45,040 --> 00:19:49,040
However, there is one certain way
to dissolve the ring without harm.

334
00:19:49,140 --> 00:19:51,980
Simply battle and defeat
me within 33 days,

335
00:19:52,160 --> 00:19:56,437
and I shall give you the antidote that
I keep inside the hollow of my lip ring.

336
00:19:56,520 --> 00:19:57,350
Jojo!

337
00:19:57,433 --> 00:20:01,300
The vow on that wedding ring
states, Till death do us part, Jojo.

338
00:20:01,820 --> 00:20:03,920
Be at the Coliseum in 33 days.

339
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:07,786
Meet me there at midnight, and
we shall battle as equals, Jojo.

340
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:12,757
I hope you didn't think your paltry
tricks would help you escape, human.

341
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:17,664
I don't imagine the two of us will fight,
but just in case, here's a gift for you.

342
00:20:18,380 --> 00:20:21,040
One that fits perfectly
around your windpipe!

343
00:20:23,300 --> 00:20:24,980
My heart and my throat!

344
00:20:25,480 --> 00:20:27,837
My poison is quite different from Wamu's,

345
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:31,214
and I keep the antidote for
that poison in my nose ring.

346
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,520
Kars, would you like to go next?

347
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:35,820
I don't think so.

348
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,657
Immortality can be boring at times.

349
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:43,740
To encounter a worthy opponent, that is
both such a rare and tantalizing thought.

350
00:20:44,060 --> 00:20:46,472
A gift that would give our lives meaning.

351
00:20:46,720 --> 00:20:48,460
I can see why you do this.

352
00:20:48,740 --> 00:20:52,297
However, do not forget that our goal
is to obtain the Red Stone of Asia.

353
00:20:52,380 --> 00:20:54,500
We must stay focused. Let's go!

354
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:59,680
Train long and hard, Jojo, so you
can challenge my divine sandstorm!

355
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:05,280
I can't believe that.

356
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:07,225
Two wedding rings with poison?

357
00:21:07,360 --> 00:21:10,137
Is that supposed to be some
kind of sick joke or something?

358
00:21:10,220 --> 00:21:13,097
I've got one around my throat
and one around my heart.

359
00:21:13,180 --> 00:21:16,533
Do these guys think I'm some
kind of bigamist or maybe...

360
00:21:20,120 --> 00:21:23,460
Well, at least Speedwagon
and Caesar are safe.

361
00:21:23,840 --> 00:21:25,252
That's what's important.

362
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:27,780
No sense in feeling sorry for myself.

363
00:21:34,480 --> 00:21:36,260
Jojo, you fool.

364
00:21:37,380 --> 00:21:40,297
That was one hell of a
bluff you just pulled there!

365
00:21:40,380 --> 00:21:43,637
The best con man couldn't
have done it better than you.

366
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,757
You acted bravely, but now
you'll need to back it up.

367
00:21:47,840 --> 00:21:50,317
We don't have much time to work.

368
00:21:50,400 --> 00:21:53,320
And we have serious Hamon training ahead.

369
00:21:55,900 --> 00:21:58,957
In and around the lake.

370
00:21:59,040 --> 00:22:02,037
Mornings come out of the sky.

371
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:04,660
They stand there.

372
00:22:06,060 --> 00:22:08,377
24 before my love?

373
00:22:08,460 --> 00:22:10,140
I'll be there.

374
00:23:29,300 --> 00:23:31,977
When I said I needed a month,
I only meant it as a blob!

375
00:23:32,060 --> 00:23:34,157
Well, from up here, it's
really more deep than tall.

376
00:23:34,240 --> 00:23:35,070
God, wait!

377
00:23:35,153 --> 00:23:35,983
Please don't do this!

378
00:23:36,066 --> 00:23:38,517
Because you're a girl doesn't mean
that I won't give you what you deserve.

379
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,659
Welcome to Venice.
